    {
        "id": "ja:word:nature-tree",
        "label": "き",
        "class": "lexical:noun",
        "fields": {
            "pronunciation": ["き"],
            "usage_notes": {
                "en": "A living woody plant. Japanese 木 here means tree, not wood as a material. き is one short mora; trees ends in /z/.",
                "de": "Eine lebende verholzte Pflanze. 木 bedeutet hier Baum, nicht Holz als Material. き ist eine kurze More; trees endet auf /z/.",
                "id": "Tumbuhan berkayu yang hidup. 木 di sini berarti pohon, bukan bahan kayu. き satu mora pendek; trees berakhir /z/.",
                "ja": "生きた樹木。ここでの木は材料の木材ではない。きは短い一拍。Trees の語尾は /z/。"
            },
            "reference_images": [
                "images/8a8968c8495e4dd37d6daa157fdf1945839c7fc62d7867a5191659602e66e117.jpg"
            ],
            "audio": "audio/2e41c2681981af9cdc96dd86bab62c17574c815262f315a50124c83009b2bc2a.wav"
        },
        "tags": ["noun", "nature"],
